SoulX-Podcast-1.7B, converted for MLX (8-bit language model) by AudioSmith
Copyright 2025 Soul AI Lab (Soul-AILab) and the SoulX-Podcast authors

This repository redistributes, in converted form, the weights of
Soul-AILab/SoulX-Podcast-1.7B (https://huggingface.co/Soul-AILab/SoulX-Podcast-1.7B,
revision 7d381e3aa4f2ac9e23201b57957fd0499f8f2fd1), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Its acoustic components (flow.pt, hift.pt, campplus.onnx) are byte-identical
to those of FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice2-0.5B (https://huggingface.co/FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice2-0.5B),
Copyright Alibaba Group (Tongyi SpeechTeam) and the CosyVoice authors, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The CAM++ speaker encoder originates
from 3D-Speaker (https://github.com/modelscope/3D-Speaker), Apache License 2.0.
The language model is a fine-tune of Qwen3-1.7B (Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud),
Apache License 2.0.

Changes made by AudioSmith (https://github.com/hehehai/AudioSmith):
  - the Qwen3 language model quantized to 8 bits (group size 64, bfloat16
    scales) with mlx-lm; its tied output layer is not stored separately;
  - flow.pt, hift.pt and campplus.onnx converted to one safetensors file
    (s3gen.safetensors, float32): modules renamed, weight norm folded,
    convolutions transposed to MLX's layout, and the batch norms the ONNX
    exporter had folded into CAM++'s convolutions written back as identity
    batch norms with the folded biases;
  - the tokenizer and configuration files are upstream's, unchanged.
The conversion is scripts/soulx/convert.py in the AudioSmith repository at
the commit recorded in conversion.json.
